# The build stage does `COPY . .`, so anything left here is uploaded to the
# builder and lands in a layer. Only what `go build ./cmd/coredhcp` reads has
# to stay: go.mod, go.sum and the Go packages under cmd/, config/, events/,
# handler/, leases/, logger/, plugins/ and server/. No package uses go:embed,
# so nothing that is not a .go file is needed at build time.

# Version control and editor state.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.golangci.yml

# Build output and coverage from a local `make`. Copying a host-built binary
# in would also bust the layer cache on every run.
bin/
coverage.out
coverage.txt
server6

# Tests never run in the image; the compose and netns harnesses under test/
# pull in configs and scripts the server itself does not read.
test/

# Docs and the screenshot the README embeds.
**/*.md
tui.png
LICENSE

# Local runtime state. A config or a lease database baked into the image would
# shadow whatever is mounted at /etc/coredhcp and /var/lib/coredhcp, and a
# leaked lease file is customer data.
.env
.env.*
**/config.yml
**/config.yaml
**/leases.txt
**/leases4.txt
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
